    nghttpx: Remove server push

commit 7cbd4f510adcdc20d813ed55ba37c13c2057183a
Author:     Tatsuhiro Tsujikawa <tatsuhiro.t@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: 2026-09-10
Commit:     Tatsuhiro Tsujikawa <tatsuhiro.t@gmail.com>
CommitDate: 2026-09-10

    nghttpx: Remove server push
    
    This change removes the server push from nghttpx.  The server push in
    HTTP/2 is particularly hard to use in practice.  No major browsers
    support it.  In tooling world, curl plans to remove it in the early
    next year.
    
    https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9113#section-8.4 describes
    the difficulties to use server push effectively.
    
    In implementation wise, it adds tremendous amount of complexities, yet
    delivers virtually no benefit at all.  It has become a maintenance
    burden.  It is a good time to remove it once and for all.  As a
    replacement, consider to use RFC 8297 "Early Hints".

